in this video you're going to learn how  to solve triangles using the law of  sines and the law of cosines so when do  you use the law of sines in law of  cosines well it's when you don't have a  right triangle and we're gonna be using  these formulas right here I'm gonna go  through two examples with you the first  one's just gonna use the law of sines  the second ones we're gonna have to use  both the law of sines and the law of  cosines so you're gonna want to see that  both of these examples the first thing  though you want to notice though is that  you see how they have this angle 97  degrees in the side across from at 8 and  here we have 40 degrees but we don't  know the side across from it so how are  we going to find this missing side well  that's where the law of sines comes in  you can use you to this top one or this  bottom one they're just reciprocals of  one another so let's go ahead and set  this up we've got the sine of 40 degrees  over its side opposite I'm going to call  that side a because it's across from  angle a and that equals the ratio of the  sine of 97 degrees over its side  opposite which is 8 so now all we have  to do is cross multiply on the diagonals  that's going to give us 8 times the sine  of 40 degrees equals a times the sine of  97 degrees to get any by itself we just  have to do the opposite of multiplying  by 97 divided by the sine of 97 and  let's see what that comes out on our  calculators now you might want to make  sure you check your mode and make sure  you're in degrees so 8 sine 40 divided  by sine of 97 and that's coming out to  about 5.2 I'm just going to round so a  equals 5.2 now when we talk about  solving triangles what that means is we  want to find all the angles and all the  sides so there's actually six pieces of  information here let's solve for this  angle see here next we have these two  angles we can add them up and subtract  from 180 to find the third so 40 plus 97  is 137 and if we subtract that from 180  we get 43 degrees okay just one side  left to solve for that's the side across  from angle C okay which is side C so you  can see we have another pair and let's  make another proportion we have sine of  43 degrees over its side opposite C  equals sine of 97 degrees over its side  opposite which is 8 now you might be  saying Mario how come you didn't use 40  and 5.2 and the reason I do that is  because five  point two we actually round in that I  answer and so if we round again on this  next step we're gonna might be a little  bit off so I tend to try to go ahead and  use the original numbers if at all  possible  so now what we're going to do is we're  just going to get C by itself and so  again I'm going to cross multiply across  that equal sign so we have C times the  sine of 97 degrees equals eight times  the sine of 43 degrees and then divide  both sides by sine of 97 degrees to get  C by itself and check my calculator work  on this we've got eight sine of 43  divided by the sine of 97 okay so I'm  getting five point five for side C and  you solve the triangle you found all the  angles all the sides  example number two we've got this side  this side and the angle in between now I  want to point out something very  important to you if you try to do the  law of sines like sine of 120 degrees  over side B and then you try to do like  the sine of angle a over like nine  you're gonna have two unknowns two  variables and you're not gonna be able  to solve that equation so we're not  gonna be able to use the law of sines on  this problem whenever they give you side  side side like three sides and nothing  else or side angle side meaning the  angle in between the two sides that's  what you're gonna have to start off by  using the law of cosines and that's  these three formulas right here so what  we're gonna do is I'm going to use this  middle formula here because I'm trying  to solve for the side across from angle  D and I know the two sides that make up  angle B so we're gonna use this middle  one I'm just gonna rewrite it real  quickly here we've got B squared equals  a squared plus C squared minus 2 AC  cosine angle B okay so now let's go  ahead and substitute in what we know so  we don't know what side B is here so  let's just leave that as B squared a is  a side across from angle a so that's  going to be 9 squared C is the one  across from angle C that's 7 squared  minus 2 times 9 times 7 times the cosine  of angle B which is 120 degrees now to  solve for B see how this is B squared we  can take the square root of both sides  and that'll be what B is now check my  work on this we're gonna do this all I'm  gonna do it all in one step on the  calculator so we're gonna take the  square root of the quantity nine squared  plus seven squared minus two times nine  times seven times the cosine of 120 and  again make sure you're in degrees I'm  getting about thirteen point nine for  side B here so let's go ahead and put  that in so now what we're gonna do is we  can switch gears we can go over to law  of sines because you can see we've got a  pair now we've got 120 and thirteen  point nine and we're gonna solve for  angle a and side nine we could do at  angle C first as well but let's just do  angle a so we've got sine of angle a  over its side opposite which is nine  equals the sine of 120 degrees over its  side opposite which is thirteen point  nine now here I'm going to do I'm gonna  get sine of a by itself I'm gonna  multiply both sides by nine to get sine  of a by itself then what we're gonna  have to do is whenever you solve for the  missing angle you're gonna have to do  the sine inverse okay of both sides so  I'm gonna figure out what this is I'm  gonna take the sine inverse of it or you  can do it all in one step I tend to do  it in two steps so we've got nine times  a sine 120 divided by thirteen point  nine and then I'm gonna do the sine  inverse of that previous answer so I try  to take that whole long decimal so I get  a little bit more accuracy I'm getting  about thirty four point one for angle a  which is right here thirty four point  one degrees now you can see we've got  two of the angles to find the third  angle all we have to do is subtract from  180 degrees let's see we get a one  hundred fifty four point one so what's a  hundred and eighty minus one hundred  fifty four point one twenty-five foot  nine and that's it so now you solve the  triangle you found all the angles all  the sides and you got it if you want to  see what happens when you have like the  potential for getting two triangles or  one triangle or even no triangle follow  me over to that video right there where  I talk about that important concept of  the ambiguous case or the side side  angle condition

